# Monthly SEO Sprint (Search Console)

Run this workflow whenever the user shares a Google Search Console report, top queries/pages, or asks for a monthly SEO sprint.

## Goal

Raise CTR and move high-impression pages from positions ~10–20 onto page 1 by upgrading the pages people already search for — not inventing random content.

## Intake

Ask for (or extract from their paste):

1. Top pages by impressions (and clicks/CTR/position if available)
2. Top queries for those pages
3. Date range of the report

Or import a Search Console export folder:

```bash
node scripts/import-gsc-export.mjs "<export-folder>" YYYY-MM
```

Snapshots live in `data/seo/search-console/` and appear in Admin → **SEO**.

Prioritize: high impressions + soft CTR and/or position 8–20.

## Per place page (top N, usually 3–5)

Use existing place JSON + `PlaceDetail` patterns (no MDX place pages).

- Expand history/legend (DOCUMENTED vs FOLKLORE) toward ~1200–2000 words where substance exists
- More H2/H3 via `##` / `###` in copy (`RichProse`)
- FAQ + FAQPage schema (`faq` field)
- Info box when key facts help (`infoBox`)
- Nearby (geo) + Related Places + breadcrumbs
- Haunted Sweden Investigation section (planned OK)
- Gallery / cover when assets exist
- Stronger meta title, description, OG, TouristAttraction JSON-LD

## Homepage (if in top impressions)

Featured, Verified, Popular, Latest, stats, and meta that name top searched places.

## Guardrails

- Official sources only for history; never present folklore as fact
- Append/enrich JSON; do not invent unverifiable events
- Prefer local `/places/*` images over fragile hotlinks
- Validate: `npm run validate:places`
- Commit/push only when the user asks

## After sprint report

Return: pages upgraded, queries targeted, meta changes, remaining cover/photo gaps, suggested next month focus.
